<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_DarkTowerControlConsole - SCALD_DARK_TOWER_1's Rust Cathedral tie.

  Owner ruling (SCALD_DARK_TOWER_1, verbatim in intent, 2026-09-07): the dark
  tower is the Rakatan's GROUND-BASED HIGH COMMAND and "has control systems
  for the Rust Cathedral in it as well." the_scald.md SS8's own amendment
  calls this a "command-and-control tie between the two sites, not a shared
  biome or roster" and leaves it explicitly open whether that tie is
  mechanical or narrative (its own "verify" line).

  THIS PASS: narrative/structural, not mechanical - and deliberately so.
  RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1 (the_rust_cathedral.md's own "C# kit" item) owns
  the hum-mood system: "a slow-moving attitude value voiced as layered tones,
  displayed by the bolts' dances, with droid commentary and hysteresis
  wiring" - and that C# is NOT YET BUILT (the item still reads as a spec).
  SCALD_DARK_TOWER_1 says explicitly: "reuse/extend that pattern rather than
  inventing a parallel one." Building a second, different attitude/mood
  system on this console to fake the tie NOW would be exactly the parallel
  system that instruction forbids. So this ThingDef is the ANCHOR POINT for
  that future wiring - the console the crew finds, the object whose label
  and description carry the tie in text - and nothing here invents new mood
  mechanics. Whoever eventually builds RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1's hum-mood
  GameComponent should hook this building (by defName or a shared tag), not
  duplicate it.

  Mechanically it is the OPPOSITE of RUT_VaultHeart (VaultDungeons/
  ThingDefs_Buildings/RUT_VaultHeart.xml) on purpose: VaultHeart is DEAD and
  needs a delivered AIPersonaCore to wake (the thaw-gate pattern shared by
  the frozen-Rakata vault and ANCIENT_WAR_LAB_1's war lab). This tower is the
  opposite case - "garrisons that never got the order to stand down"
  (SCALD_DARK_TOWER_1, echoing the_forgotten_war.md R-W1's self-replicating
  defensive systems) means the whole site, console included, is ALREADY
  LIVE on arrival. No thaw trigger, no delivered item, no dormant state.
  That is the mechanical fact that keeps this site distinct from both other
  dungeons in the arc (ANCIENT_WAR_LAB_1's frozen approach/thaw-gate;
  VAULT_DUNGEON_BUILD_1 type (3)'s dark, frost-locked, needs-a-core scene).

  CompPowerPlant (negative consumption = a SOURCE, already running, no fuel
  comp at all - "the pumps still run") feeds the core's own point-defense
  ring through KCSG's spawnConduits (see StructureLayoutDefs_DarkTower.xml),
  same wiring shape as RUT_VaultHeart's circuit but never dead to begin with.
  Not buildable, not deconstructible (ancient, and the whole point of the
  fierce garrison outside is that nobody gets close enough to try), claimable
  once the garrison is cleared - a study prize, not a resource.

  Art is the same vanilla ship-computer-core placeholder RUT_VaultHeart uses;
  no new art authored this pass.
-->
<Defs>
  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase">
    <defName>RUT_DarkTowerControlConsole</defName>
    <label>high command console</label>
    <description>A Forsaken command console, still drawing power after all this time. Its data-spikes run to a socket built for interfaces that no longer exist - and among the runs still live, the fittings match nothing found anywhere else on the plateau except the Rust Cathedral itself.\n\nThis was the Rakata's ground-based high command. Whatever it commanded is not obvious from the console alone.</description>
    <thingClass>Building</thingClass>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Ship/ShipComputerCore</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(1.6,1.6)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <fillPercent>1</fillPercent>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <size>(1,1)</size>
    <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>1000</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <Beauty>-5</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <building>
      <deconstructible>false</deconstructible>
      <claimable>true</claimable>
    </building>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Power">
        <compClass>CompPowerPlant</compClass>
        <basePowerConsumption>-1200</basePowerConsumption>
        <transmitsPower>true</transmitsPower>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Glower">
        <glowRadius>9</glowRadius>
        <glowColor>(180,220,255,0)</glowColor>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>
</Defs>
